# 3. CONVEX BACKEND CONNECTION

Use a single Convex client throughout the React application.

Configure:

`src/main.tsx`

```tsx
import React from "react";
import ReactDOM from "react-dom/client";
import {
  ConvexProvider,
  ConvexReactClient,
} from "convex/react";

import App from "./App";

const url = import.meta.env.VITE_CONVEX_URL;

if (!url) {
  throw new Error("Missing VITE_CONVEX_URL");
}

const convex = new ConvexReactClient(url);

ReactDOM.createRoot(
  document.getElementById("root")!
).render(
  <React.StrictMode>
    <ConvexProvider client={convex}>
      <App />
    </ConvexProvider>
  </React.StrictMode>
);
```

If using an authentication integration requiring a specialized provider, replace the provider wiring with the officially documented authenticated variant.

Create backend code under:

`convex/`

Use generated Convex API references:

`convex/_generated/api`

Frontend data retrieval must use:

`useQuery()`

Frontend database mutations must use:

`useMutation()`

External service operations must use appropriate Convex actions or HTTP actions.

Do not use generic HTTP API calls where the native Convex client is the better option.

